WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:04.480
Once there was an adventurer
party called the Silver Tigers.

00:05.030 --> 00:08.730
Their leader, Bishot, was a man of
rare intelligence for a Tigerian.

00:08.730 --> 00:11.060
He was my older brother.

00:11.850 --> 00:14.010
The Mechasteel Moonhell...

00:14.010 --> 00:17.800
That Labyrinth was like a living
creature that sought out our blood,

00:17.800 --> 00:21.290
and our lives, and stole
them without remorse.

00:25.910 --> 00:28.310
But we wouldn't let that
place get away with it.

00:28.750 --> 00:33.130
We found "them", we defeated them,
and stole everything they had.

00:33.510 --> 00:37.760
And without his genius,
that would've been impossible.

00:38.290 --> 00:41.310
He attained every kind of
wealth and fame imaginable,

00:41.310 --> 00:43.410
and died just like you'd expect him to.

00:44.060 --> 00:48.650
A small, miserable death, without
a trace of intelligence or dignity.

00:49.300 --> 00:50.900
And that's why I thought to myself...

00:52.020 --> 00:54.860
You can't believe in humanity!

01:08.360 --> 01:10.380
Start talking.

01:10.380 --> 01:15.820
No one ever saw a trace of the treasures
you stole, not even on the black market.

01:15.820 --> 01:18.190
I have one special secret.

01:19.110 --> 01:20.680
You have it with you, don't you?

01:21.250 --> 01:24.810
One of the things we stole from
the labyrinth that night...

01:24.810 --> 01:26.300
How'd you figure it out?

01:27.500 --> 01:29.370
You've decided to start talking?

01:29.370 --> 01:30.940
If you hadn't figured it out,

01:30.940 --> 01:33.780
you would've lived to have a nice
drink at the tavern tomorrow.

01:34.720 --> 01:38.930
A treasure that was too dangerous
to sell, and too dangerous to use.

01:40.370 --> 01:41.990
Come forth! Sword of Destruction!

01:43.860 --> 01:47.590
Life's a gamble, people say.

01:47.590 --> 01:49.620
And that's true for us Tigerians, too.

01:50.250 --> 01:53.230
Tonight, my gamble was that...

01:54.000 --> 02:05.810
Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World

03:24.460 --> 03:25.810
I don't like it.

03:24.760 --> 03:29.680
"Gambling Lesson"

03:26.780 --> 03:27.820
The wealthy patron.

03:27.820 --> 03:29.880
Dealer! Hurry it up!

03:28.990 --> 03:30.810
And I'm calling him Mr. Gigolo.

03:31.280 --> 03:32.800
Of course.

03:32.800 --> 03:34.690
And then the dealer who's robbing him blind,

03:35.090 --> 03:38.990
along with the small-time shark who
wants to make some pocket change.

03:39.470 --> 03:41.170
I don't like it.

03:43.630 --> 03:45.580
I'll have no problems crushing them all.

03:55.170 --> 03:57.640
There's a reason we're here.

03:57.640 --> 03:59.870
After the Mathematics Bare Knuckle,

03:59.870 --> 04:02.670
we made some decent cash
and split up to take a break.

04:02.130 --> 04:05.140
Infuriated Grape Ice Cream

04:02.670 --> 04:04.790
Infuriated Grape Ice Cream?

04:04.790 --> 04:07.650
The ice cream at the casino's
supposed to be really good.

04:08.140 --> 04:12.010
I'm willing to take you there,
but once we arrive, we split up.

04:12.590 --> 04:14.990
I'm basically here to watch over Kizuna.

04:14.440 --> 04:17.150
Sold Out

04:14.990 --> 04:16.580
Okay, we're all sold out!

04:16.580 --> 04:19.130
What? What's going on?

04:19.130 --> 04:21.380
Do you know how long
I've been in this line?

04:20.880 --> 04:23.030
Please come back soon!

04:23.030 --> 04:25.970
How <i>dare</i> you treat me like this?!

04:25.970 --> 04:28.740
Just you wait! I'll be back!

04:28.740 --> 04:30.020
We'll be waiting!

04:31.830 --> 04:35.100
Crap. We didn't get what we came for.

04:35.100 --> 04:38.120
Since you're here,
why not enjoy some gambling?

04:38.120 --> 04:42.410
I can't gamble.
I have ethics rules installed.

04:43.430 --> 04:46.170
Wow, look! Anti-magic paint!

04:46.170 --> 04:47.460
You're correct.

04:47.460 --> 04:52.410
Everything used in our games
has anti-magic on it.

04:52.920 --> 04:56.780
That's an expensive way to stop cheaters.

04:56.780 --> 04:58.110
Thank you.

04:58.690 --> 05:04.190
WELCOME

05:01.720 --> 05:04.190
Where are you, Nick?

05:04.580 --> 05:07.380
I can smell you!

05:24.990 --> 05:28.410
They want me to join in and take
some money from Mr. Gigolo, too?

05:28.410 --> 05:31.220
I see. They're making it pretty obvious.

05:33.630 --> 05:35.990
Sure, I'm in.

05:35.990 --> 05:38.980
In the end, I'll take you all
for everything you've got.

05:39.370 --> 05:42.860
But right now, it's Mr. Gigolo I don't like.

05:53.930 --> 05:54.750
Damn it!

05:54.750 --> 05:56.510
You tricked me!

05:56.780 --> 05:57.930
Tricked?

05:57.930 --> 06:00.010
Who tricked who?

06:01.210 --> 06:04.370
Don't be silly.
That's why we're all here, right?

06:04.370 --> 06:07.390
You've got no talent for gambling.

06:07.390 --> 06:10.040
Or rather, you're no gambler.

06:10.680 --> 06:11.770
What?

06:12.130 --> 06:13.990
If you can't play with your own money,

06:13.990 --> 06:16.380
then go home and bet with your
friends for penny candy.

06:22.700 --> 06:28.640
U-Um, are you trying to get him to give up?

06:28.640 --> 06:34.870
No real gambler would pass up the
opportunity to take three easy marks.

06:36.420 --> 06:38.140
Thanks.

06:39.800 --> 06:42.560
I'm not one to tell other people
how to live their lives...

06:42.970 --> 06:44.230
But why not ditch the guy?

06:45.580 --> 06:49.030
Is it that easy to throw someone aside?

06:49.980 --> 06:51.140
It is.

06:51.540 --> 06:53.550
Both throwing someone away,
and being thrown away.

06:54.480 --> 06:57.070
Is that true?

06:57.070 --> 06:59.300
Knowing when to give up is
what makes a good gambler.

06:59.300 --> 07:02.320
Once you get attached,
you start making mistakes.

07:02.320 --> 07:05.240
Will I ever be able to be a gambler?

07:05.910 --> 07:07.560
You already are, right?

07:09.110 --> 07:12.520
Some guys will keep betting on the dark
horse, and then win big in the end.

07:16.540 --> 07:17.840
Wh-What?

07:18.540 --> 07:20.880
A-A monster!

07:20.880 --> 07:21.590
Donny?

07:21.590 --> 07:22.730
It'll eat me!

07:22.740 --> 07:23.980
A monster!

07:25.550 --> 07:26.710
A monster?

07:30.370 --> 07:31.840
Nick!

07:33.090 --> 07:35.050
Come on out, Nick!

07:35.870 --> 07:39.480
What am I doing?

07:39.900 --> 07:42.200
Where am I?

07:43.910 --> 07:47.190
I'm just looking for Nick...

07:48.400 --> 07:50.430
I realized...

07:50.430 --> 07:52.660
On that day, I realized...

07:53.810 --> 07:57.400
Yeah. He never despaired.

07:58.330 --> 08:02.370
I hated him. I was jealous of him.
I was envious of him.

08:02.730 --> 08:05.750
I wanted to be like him.
I was miserable because of him.

08:06.530 --> 08:07.790
I don't even know...

08:08.150 --> 08:12.560
I can't even remember which of
those feelings were real anymore.

08:23.350 --> 08:24.780
Well?

08:24.780 --> 08:27.630
This is what you wanted, right?

08:28.470 --> 08:30.430
It's been a long, long time, Leon.

08:30.430 --> 08:32.660
Are you finally ready to use me?

08:33.390 --> 08:35.530
There's a man I want to kill.

08:35.530 --> 08:37.670
The pants-pisser here?

08:38.300 --> 08:41.290
No, he's not here.

08:41.730 --> 08:44.580
You remember his smell, right?

08:44.580 --> 08:48.540
Yeah, I'll never be able to
forget that awful scent.

08:48.900 --> 08:55.700
Then I'll evolve your senses, so that you
can find him with your own sense of smell.

08:55.700 --> 08:57.960
The wonders of modern technology, huh?

08:57.960 --> 09:02.050
Don't be silly. This technology
is hundreds of years old.

09:02.400 --> 09:05.050
You've all regressed greatly.

09:05.700 --> 09:07.180
I'm joking.

09:09.540 --> 09:10.700
Evolution!

09:17.330 --> 09:19.460
Where are you, Nick?

09:22.490 --> 09:24.950
His smell's coming from this way?

09:27.440 --> 09:29.310
What's a monster doing in the casino?

09:29.700 --> 09:30.830
This is bad.

09:31.250 --> 09:34.210
I handed over my weapons when I came in.

09:34.210 --> 09:37.210
That smell... I know you.

09:37.210 --> 09:39.460
You were with him, weren't you?

09:39.460 --> 09:41.560
S-Someone you know?

09:41.560 --> 09:42.560
No!

09:42.560 --> 09:44.110
Where's Nick?

09:44.420 --> 09:46.830
Nick? You mean that Nick?

09:46.830 --> 09:49.340
That shithead Nick!

09:49.340 --> 09:50.720
The one who's big into idols?

09:50.720 --> 09:55.110
The one who set us up in the
Mathematics Bare Knuckle!

09:55.110 --> 09:57.740
The one who complains about
little stuff far too much?

09:57.740 --> 09:59.500
He definitely is someone you know, right?

09:59.500 --> 10:03.630
The one who kept calling me a kitty!

10:03.630 --> 10:06.020
Which means you're...

10:06.020 --> 10:06.960
Someone she knows!

10:06.960 --> 10:08.000
I'm Leon!

10:08.000 --> 10:09.950
You're <i>that</i> Leon?

10:08.790 --> 10:11.380
See? I knew you knew him.

10:11.380 --> 10:14.250
You've changed a lot since I last saw you.

10:15.030 --> 10:16.620
What do you want with Nick?

10:16.620 --> 10:19.640
What else? I want to break him in half.

10:20.000 --> 10:22.820
And you think I'll hand him over?

10:22.820 --> 10:24.630
That's up to you.

10:24.970 --> 10:30.670
I'm curious to see which you value more:
your own life or Nick's.

10:30.670 --> 10:34.450
What do you expect me to say?
My life or Nick's...

10:34.450 --> 10:37.410
Hey, choose your next words carefully.

10:37.410 --> 10:43.790
My enhanced sense of smell
can even sniff out lies.

10:44.090 --> 10:49.230
The second I know you're lying, you're
going to end up a stain on the carpet.

10:54.030 --> 10:55.780
It's pretty loud out there.

10:57.540 --> 10:59.080
What's going on?!

11:00.240 --> 11:02.600
My life or Nick's...

11:03.200 --> 11:06.800
It's a stupid question.
One with only one answer.

11:06.800 --> 11:12.670
But if I say it, I'll end
up as a carpet stain.

11:13.110 --> 11:15.070
I'm sure of it.

11:22.990 --> 11:24.270
Hey, you.

11:25.260 --> 11:28.210
Why did you think you could
use me as a hostage?

11:28.630 --> 11:33.330
What? Because if I threaten the
life of one of his comrades...

11:34.000 --> 11:35.320
What's so funny?

11:35.580 --> 11:37.360
Comrades, huh?

11:37.880 --> 11:41.930
So does that mean, even to a villain
like you, we look like comrades?

11:41.930 --> 11:43.550
What are you saying?

11:43.550 --> 11:45.590
We're not comrades.

11:45.590 --> 11:47.800
None of us trust each other.

11:47.800 --> 11:52.270
We're a group of adventures who don't
believe in humanity, or each other.

11:52.730 --> 11:55.600
You can't believe in humanity!

11:55.600 --> 11:58.130
I see... comrades, huh?

12:01.010 --> 12:02.980
Do you understand the situation you're in?

12:03.390 --> 12:04.950
Of course I do.

12:06.830 --> 12:10.750
I guess we do look like
comrades, then? That's funny.

12:11.310 --> 12:12.660
You...

12:17.090 --> 12:20.100
This is pretty pricey stuff.

12:20.100 --> 12:22.860
The pipe's made from a spirit tree.

12:22.860 --> 12:25.800
And the leaves are specially
grown in the south.

12:26.810 --> 12:29.170
I guess this is my last smoke, though.

12:29.790 --> 12:33.010
Oh, right.
This igniter's a little different.

12:33.270 --> 12:37.370
It's got a special thing where you
can disable the limiter and...

12:37.370 --> 12:38.440
Lightning Flash!

12:46.500 --> 12:49.000
And you can do little attacks with it!

12:55.720 --> 12:57.030
Crap!

12:57.440 --> 12:59.920
Once something changes, it never
goes back to how it was before.

12:59.920 --> 13:02.060
That's what my brother always said.

13:02.590 --> 13:06.810
That was a big burn...
and it's already healed?

13:06.810 --> 13:09.540
That just now told me how you really feel.

13:12.270 --> 13:13.570
You there!

13:14.300 --> 13:17.070
She's your money ticket, right? Protect her!

13:17.550 --> 13:18.600
Quickly!

13:23.620 --> 13:27.870
I-I'm not with Bell for the money!

13:28.350 --> 13:29.570
Hurry!

13:31.380 --> 13:36.060
We're not comrades like you think.

13:36.960 --> 13:39.260
We're just people who've lost everything,

13:39.260 --> 13:42.720
leaning on each other to keep
from collapsing entirely.

13:43.010 --> 13:46.500
We'd never help each other if it meant we
had to risk something that mattered to us.

13:46.500 --> 13:47.710
What?

13:49.150 --> 13:51.440
I don't smell a lie.

13:51.440 --> 13:53.640
She means it...

13:53.640 --> 13:55.590
No, this is...

13:55.990 --> 13:59.570
The smell of hope and resignation.

13:59.570 --> 14:00.970
Pathetic.

14:00.970 --> 14:05.100
I guarantee to you that even if you take
me hostage, Nick won't come for me!

14:06.820 --> 14:07.740
Then...

14:08.390 --> 14:09.970
die!

14:12.040 --> 14:14.710
Oh, a big cat.

14:17.110 --> 14:18.570
You know this guy?

14:21.240 --> 14:22.550
That's right.

14:22.550 --> 14:24.910
I can't have you dying on me.

14:25.670 --> 14:27.800
'Cause having you around is to my benefit.

14:30.500 --> 14:32.610
So you finally came, huh?

14:32.610 --> 14:35.000
Hey there, big cat.

14:35.000 --> 14:36.960
You haven't changed.

14:36.960 --> 14:39.570
Nick, be careful!
He's not who he used to be.

14:39.570 --> 14:40.800
Used to be?

14:41.760 --> 14:44.570
Do I know any big cats?

14:44.570 --> 14:48.440
You do! I used to be a kitty!

14:48.440 --> 14:51.340
So you've started admitting it.

14:51.780 --> 14:53.070
You knew who I was!

14:54.460 --> 14:56.330
Wait, Leon.

14:57.190 --> 14:58.690
There's one more here.

14:58.690 --> 14:59.640
What?

14:59.640 --> 15:01.930
There's one more here.

15:01.930 --> 15:03.200
What did you say?

15:04.010 --> 15:06.240
You've finally noticed, huh?

15:06.240 --> 15:09.710
So it's you, Sword of Bonds!

15:09.710 --> 15:12.710
I should've known it would
be you, Sword of Evolution.

15:12.710 --> 15:15.350
Hey, who are you talking to?

15:15.740 --> 15:17.840
He's talking to his sword, too?

15:17.840 --> 15:19.410
He should be.

15:19.410 --> 15:22.530
But the owner is only barely
keeping the sword under control.

15:22.530 --> 15:24.790
It's been centuries since last we met.

15:24.790 --> 15:27.240
Begone instead of trying to get in my way.

15:27.240 --> 15:29.330
That's not possible.

15:29.330 --> 15:32.620
Then, I'll get rid of you by force.

15:32.620 --> 15:35.990
Leon, I'll bestow upon you my full grace!

15:35.990 --> 15:38.300
Irrational Moonlight!

15:43.170 --> 15:44.240
You're kidding!

15:44.240 --> 15:46.120
He got bigger again!

15:46.120 --> 15:48.550
That's crazy! His wielder
won't survive that!

15:48.880 --> 15:52.630
He's swallowing up not just
their body, but their mind, too.

15:52.910 --> 15:54.300
Hey, big cat!

15:54.300 --> 15:58.040
If you get too big, you won't fit on
the roof when you go to sunbathe!

16:00.070 --> 16:01.660
We can't even talk to him, huh?

16:01.660 --> 16:03.770
Kizuna! Union!

16:04.540 --> 16:05.640
Will it work?

16:05.640 --> 16:07.560
Try it!

16:11.210 --> 16:12.290
Okay...

16:12.290 --> 16:13.450
Union!

16:30.270 --> 16:32.430
Wh-What is that?

16:33.670 --> 16:34.660
Who is that?

16:35.170 --> 16:36.560
Ice Age!

16:38.890 --> 16:40.800
It's so cold! What is this?

16:44.010 --> 16:45.210
Ice Shield!

16:50.730 --> 16:51.930
It's not working, huh?

16:54.660 --> 16:57.510
No... What am I doing?

16:57.510 --> 17:00.190
Why am I doing this?

17:00.750 --> 17:04.210
I won't make any money...
I won't make anyone happy...

17:04.590 --> 17:07.070
This isn't what I wanted to do!

17:09.940 --> 17:10.700
Stop it!

17:11.260 --> 17:14.830
I just wanted to rough him up a little bit!

17:15.390 --> 17:16.580
I sent people flying.

17:17.080 --> 17:19.590
Guards, innocent women, and children alike.

17:19.970 --> 17:21.780
These expensive-looking decorations...

17:21.780 --> 17:24.850
This place where everyone has fun...
I've wrecked it all!

17:24.850 --> 17:26.030
That's right.

17:26.030 --> 17:30.730
Your power can destroy a place that was once
filled with smiles with a single strike.

17:31.010 --> 17:32.560
It's fun, isn't it?

17:32.560 --> 17:34.740
To have overwhelming power.

17:35.080 --> 17:38.620
Look. Everyone is in awe of your power.

17:38.620 --> 17:43.230
They flee, knowing that death
awaits them at any moment!

17:45.760 --> 17:47.830
Stop it! Stop!

17:47.830 --> 17:52.620
It's too late.
This is what you've always done.

17:53.600 --> 17:54.650
Ice Shield!

18:00.090 --> 18:04.820
When you took me from the Mechasteel
Moonhell Labyrinth on that day,

18:04.820 --> 18:07.380
you were already like this.

18:07.650 --> 18:10.220
That's why you were able to hold me.

18:10.220 --> 18:11.410
No!

18:11.410 --> 18:15.980
I just wanted to be an
adventurer, like my brother!

18:15.980 --> 18:18.280
But he's dead.

18:18.530 --> 18:19.530
Ice Spear!

18:21.830 --> 18:26.040
That's right! He was killed by assholes
who I thought were comrades!

18:26.040 --> 18:31.200
A bunch of cowards who he did everything for,

18:31.200 --> 18:33.170
but who couldn't do anything without him!

18:33.170 --> 18:34.340
That's right.

18:34.340 --> 18:36.670
That's why you hate people.

18:36.670 --> 18:38.840
I had the right to!

18:38.840 --> 18:39.930
Sure you had the right.

18:40.220 --> 18:44.060
And then, little by little,
you loosened the rules,

18:44.330 --> 18:47.510
until you had the right
to look down on everyone!

18:47.510 --> 18:50.800
Life's easy when you're better
than everyone else, right?

18:51.130 --> 18:54.380
'Cause you don't need to think
about anything more than that.

18:54.380 --> 18:57.400
That's how I justified it.

18:58.080 --> 19:00.130
When someone tricked me, it was their fault,

19:00.130 --> 19:04.320
but when I tricked someone,
it was also their fault.

19:04.320 --> 19:06.190
That's why you were chosen!

19:06.190 --> 19:09.480
And you grew up just like I hoped!

19:09.480 --> 19:10.400
You're wrong!

19:10.400 --> 19:11.830
I'm not.

19:12.220 --> 19:16.950
My powers will never evolve in a
way their bearer doesn't want.

19:17.560 --> 19:21.710
I wasn't a bad guy from the start, either!

19:26.220 --> 19:28.100
I'm not a bad guy!

19:28.100 --> 19:31.610
This is what you wanted, Leon!

19:31.610 --> 19:32.750
Stop it!

19:33.100 --> 19:34.850
Somebody stop me!

19:35.490 --> 19:38.990
Somebody... save me!

19:42.130 --> 19:43.250
Nick...

19:47.110 --> 19:48.320
Who's there?

19:48.320 --> 19:50.040
Don't get in my way!

19:50.040 --> 19:54.870
I have to evolve him into
the strongest hero!

19:55.640 --> 20:00.280
Stop it!

20:01.680 --> 20:02.960
Ice Coffin!

20:06.390 --> 20:10.890
The anti-magic paint on these cards
deflected the magic of the Sword of Destruction.

20:11.210 --> 20:16.650
With the light that brings evolution sealed,
its wielder is cut off from those blessings.

20:17.010 --> 20:19.910
Simple, but very clever.

20:29.790 --> 20:31.110
Thank you...

20:37.850 --> 20:40.140
The same thing happens every time.

20:41.330 --> 20:43.610
I'm a small-time villain.

20:44.170 --> 20:47.560
My whole life's been this revolving cycle.

20:47.830 --> 20:49.970
We're just people who've lost everything,

20:49.970 --> 20:53.560
leaning on each other to keep
from collapsing entirely.

20:54.420 --> 20:56.270
Stupid girl...

20:56.270 --> 20:59.010
That's what a comrade is, right?

20:59.010 --> 21:00.130
You have a visitor.

21:02.590 --> 21:05.520
You come to see the tiger
in his cage at the zoo?

21:05.900 --> 21:06.570
Yup.

21:08.160 --> 21:09.940
He's lost a lot of weight in a short time.

21:10.500 --> 21:14.400
His race is tough, but that wasn't
the only reason he was strong.

21:14.880 --> 21:19.510
He was only able to buy time in our
fight because he trained every day.

21:19.950 --> 21:21.600
It's a waste.

21:23.380 --> 21:26.900
The building's a mess, but nobody died.

21:29.180 --> 21:31.620
So I should've smashed the place up more?

21:31.620 --> 21:32.620
Maybe.

21:32.620 --> 21:34.880
You'll get out of shape
fast in a place like this.

21:37.480 --> 21:39.370
I sealed that sword away.

21:40.350 --> 21:42.350
So that blonde girl was...

21:42.900 --> 21:45.580
We've got a secret between
just the two of us, huh?

21:45.580 --> 21:46.880
I see...

21:48.360 --> 21:49.860
That woman was...

21:49.860 --> 21:51.340
Don't tell anyone.

21:51.870 --> 21:53.270
Oh...

21:53.270 --> 21:57.100
I thought it was weird that
anybody but you could beat me.

21:59.840 --> 22:00.970
Nick.

22:03.430 --> 22:06.650
You can't get drunk on beer you paid for
with money earned from lying, right?

22:10.330 --> 22:11.630
I'm sure.

23:35.010 --> 23:40.020
Next time:
"The Beautiful Paladin"

23:36.140 --> 23:39.140
Next time: "The Beautiful Paladin".
